            self.platform_name = PLATFORM_NAMES.get(kwargs["sat_id"], kwargs["sat_id"])
        except KeyError:
            # NWCSAF/PPS
            self.platform_name = kwargs["platform_name"]
            self.pps = True

        self.sensor = set([SENSOR.get(self.platform_name, "seviri")])
```

If `kwargs["sat_id"]` is "METOP-SG-A1", `PLATFORM_NAMES.get("METOP-SG-A1", "METOP-SG-A1")` returns "METOP-SG-A1".
Then `SENSOR.get("METOP-SG-A1", "seviri")` returns "seviri" because `SENSOR` has "Metop-SG-A1".

I should normalize the platform name for the `SENSOR` lookup.

